From: Bryan B <bbigari@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 01:59:38 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/5] Add AI search signal classifiers and GA4 AI referral
 service
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Two halves of the same question — where an agency shows up in AI-driven
search — kept deliberately separate because their evidence differs.

ai-referrers.ts is measurement: GA4 records the referring host, so a session
attributed to ChatGPT really came from ChatGPT. It still undercounts, because
assistants that strip the referrer land in Direct, so the service reports that
limit alongside the numbers rather than leaving callers to assume a total.

ai-query-signals.ts is inference: Google exposes no AI search type and no AI
searchAppearance, so the only signal is query text. It scores syntax a person
would not type (exact-match quotes, markdown, operators) rather than length,
because assistant queries are frequently short — AI Mode logs conversational
follow-ups as fresh searches — and length would both miss those and flag
ordinary long-tail.

Patterns are sent to Google as RE2 and run locally as JS RegExp, so they stay
in the subset both accept; a test enforces that.

